-- assert(cond): stops the program when cond is false, with the place and the call as written.
-- In a function body it runs in the program; at module level the compiler runs it, and a false
-- condition is a compile error there (docs/comptime.md §3.5). It returns cond.
-- `site: site` is filled by the compiler at each call: `file:line:col: assert(n < 4)`.
bool assert(bool true, site: site): true
bool assert(bool ok, site: site) {
    trap(site, " is false\n")
    return ok
}
